# Lab Report: API Calling to ChatGPT

## 1. Objective
The objective of this lab was to build an automated product listing generator using the OpenAI API and Python.

## 2. Implementation
The application loads product data from a Hugging Face dataset, processes product images, and sends image and text inputs to an AI model. The model generates product titles, descriptions, features, and SEO keywords.

## 3. API Integration
The OpenAI Python library was used to send requests to the model and retrieve generated responses. The responses were parsed as JSON and saved to `generated_listings.json`.

## 4. Error Handling
The application uses exception handling to record failed product requests and continues processing the remaining products. Errors are saved in `errors.json`.

## 5. Results
The application successfully generated listings for three products: a shirt, jeans, and a watch. The generated listings include a title, description, features, and keywords.

## 6. Limitations and Improvements
Some product attributes may not be verifiable from images alone. Human review is necessary before publication. Future improvements include stronger output validation, API retry logic, and usage-cost monitoring.

## 7. Conclusion
This lab demonstrated how Python and an AI API can automate product content generation through dataset loading, image processing, prompt engineering, and structured JSON output.
